      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "Describe the set $S={…,-2,-1,0,1,2,3}$ using a conditional definition.",
      "worked_solution": "The set $S$ contains all integers less than $3,$ including $3.$\n\nIn other words, $S$ contains all integers less than $4,$  *excluding* $4.$ \n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,x<4}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example:\n\n- We can write $x\\le 3.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,x\\le 3}.\n$$",
